The InstructionSet class is used to store the instructions supported by the MS51FB9AE/8051 simulator. It keeps the instruction names and their categories in a HashMap, such as Data Transfer, Arithmetic, Logical, Control Flow, and Bit Operation. HALT is also included as a simulator-specific instruction.
The decode() method reads an instruction and separates the mnemonic and its operands. For example, MOV A, #05 is separated into MOV and A, #05. It also checks whether the instruction is supported and converts it to uppercase.
The class also provides methods like isSupported(), getCategory(), and getInstructionInfo() to get basic information about an instruction. Overall, this class helps the simulator identify and organize instructions before they are executed.
